# The server log and its rotated archives. The _DEBUG variant
# contains conversation content in the clear and must never be committed.
#
# 🔴 THE SECOND LINE IS NOT REDUNDANT, AND THE REASON IT EXISTS IS A NEAR MISS. `*.log` matches only
# names ENDING in `.log`, so it covers `st_DEBUG.log` and misses `st_DEBUG.log.pre-gate3-20260721` —
# the diagnostic-snapshot convention this work uses constantly moves `.log` out of final position and
# silently leaves the copy untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add -A` away from a commit. Found on
# the AMD test host install 2026-07-21 with two plaintext debug copies and a pre-redaction copy of st.log
# exposed that way. A commit is not undone by `rm`: the blob survives deletion, survives a later
# ignore fix, and if pushed it is on GitHub in the repository whose entire purpose is that this
# content stays encrypted at rest.
*.log
*.log.*
# Same failure, applied to the files that carry credentials rather than conversations. `/config.yaml`
# is anchored and exact, so every `config.yaml.bak-pre-debugoff-20260721` was a config full of tokens
# and proxy credentials sitting unignored beside it.
config.yaml.*
secrets.json.*
providers.json.*
# 🔴 THE RULE THAT REPLACES ALL OF THE ABOVE: PRESERVE DIAGNOSTIC COPIES IN `temp/`, NOT BESIDE THE
# ORIGINAL. Every pattern above exists because a snapshot was named by appending a suffix, which moved
# the real extension out of final position and slipped past the glob that was supposed to catch it.
# Chasing that with one more pattern per suffix style is whack-a-mole and eventually misses one — and
# the thing it misses is a plaintext chat log in a repository that exists to keep chats encrypted.
# `temp/` ends the game: the directory is ignored wholesale, so ANY filename inside it is safe, and no
# future snapshot needs a new rule. `cp st_DEBUG.log temp/pre-gate3-20260721.log` and move on.
# README.md is the one tracked file, so the folder exists in a fresh clone and explains itself.
/temp/*
!/temp/README.md
/vectors/
/cache/
public/css/user.css
public/error/
/plugins/
